From: claude <claude@p7x.dev>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 22:39:31 +0000
Subject: [freebsd-ports PATCH] net-mgmt/signoz: Observability platform for
 logs, metrics, and traces
To: Pat Maddox <pat@patmaddox.com>
Cc: lab-devel@p7x.dev

SigNoz is an open source observability platform. It brings logs,
metrics, and traces together in one application, with dashboards,
alerts, exceptions, and service maps. It is native to OpenTelemetry and
stores its data in ClickHouse.

This is the Community Edition of the query service and web interface.
Telemetry reaches ClickHouse through the SigNoz distribution of the
OpenTelemetry Collector, which is packaged separately.

WWW: https://signoz.io/
---
Notes for review:

Version: v0.145.0 is the newest GitHub release and is not marked as a
pre-release. Upstream publishes no registry release other than the Go
module proxy, which has the same tag.

Edition: the port builds ./cmd/community, which is MIT. The source
also carries ee/ and cmd/enterprise/ under a separate license. The
community command imports nothing from ee/, so LICENSE=MIT holds for
what is built and installed.

Mechanism: USES=go:modules with GO_MODULE from the module proxy, the
way about 440 of the 559 GO_MODULE ports fetch. The web interface is a
pnpm and Vite build with no offline path in the tree, so the port
takes the prebuilt web/ from upstream's community release tarball,
following www/grafana, www/opengist, and net-mgmt/prometheus3. That
tarball is 70 MB and also holds a Linux binary, which is not used.
Only the linux_amd64 asset is fetched; web/ is identical across
architectures. Its name has no version, but go.mk puts every distfile
in a per-version DIST_SUBDIR, as for www/adguardhome. Its sha256
matches upstream's signoz-community_0.145.0_checksums.txt.

Plist: web/ is about 4,200 files with content hashes in their names,
so post-install appends it to TMPPLIST, as www/grafana does. Source
maps (*.map, 31 MB of the 54 MB) are left out; the UI does not need
them.

Paths: the binary's built-in defaults point at /etc/signoz/web,
/root/templates, and /var/lib/signoz. post-patch rewrites them to
DATADIR and /var/db/signoz, so "signoz server" runs with no config
file. conf/example.yaml gets the same rewrite and is installed to
DATADIR as the reference for all settings. portlint warns about the
absolute /var/db path; net-mgmt/prometheus3 does the same for its
database directory.

rc.d: modeled on net-mgmt/prometheus3's script. Configuration is the
upstream style of SIGNOZ_* environment variables through signoz_env,
with signoz_config optional. pkg-message points out that pprof (6060)
and metrics (9090, the Prometheus default) listen on all interfaces
by default, and how to change that.

UIDs/GIDs: signoz takes 404, the lowest number free in both files.

Runtime dependencies: none. ClickHouse may be remote, so it is not a
RUN_DEPENDS; pkg-message names databases/clickhouse. The schema
migrator and the collector belong to the separate otel collector port.

Version stamping: ldflags set variant, version, and the short commit
hash (GIT_HASH), as upstream's Makefile does. Build time and branch
are left unset so the build is reproducible.

Checked: portclippy and portfmt -D are clean. portlint -A has only
the /var/db warning above. makesum fetched all three distfiles; patch
ran, and each REINPLACE changed its target. The rc.d script passes
sh -n.

Not checked: Go is not installed in this jail. go-post-fetch (the
module download), vendoring, the build, stage, and the plist were not
run. makesum ran with NO_DEPENDS=yes and GO_CMD=/usr/bin/true, which
skips only the module download; distinfo does not cover modules. I
have not checked whether modernc.org/sqlite and the other dependencies
build on every architecture, so the port has no ONLY_FOR_ARCHS yet.
SigNoz was not run.

